    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d230">

                <pb facs="0179" n="170" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg170"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/1544: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-17T18:00:00+02:00">October 17, 1940—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4356. Department’s 2734, October 15, 6 p.m., and my 3835, August 31, noon.
                    American citizens in Germany are having no difficulty in obtaining exit visas
                    but except in rare instances are not being allowed to purchase foreign exchange
                    unless they are able to show that they brought the exchange into Germany with
                    them or unless the funds come within the purview of the German assurances with
                    respect to inheritance transfers.</p>
                <p>There has been no recent information from Brussels or Rotterdam regarding the
                    departure of American citizens and the Consuls in those two cities are being
                    requested to report.<anchor n="70" xml:id="d230-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d230-f1" n="70" xml:id="d230-f1-content">
                <p>In despatch No. 434, November 7, the Vice Consul at Brussels reported that the
                    first group of Americans left Brussels en route for Lisbon on October 22 but
                    that various difficulties regarding money and Spanish visas continued.</p>
                <p>In despatch No. 753, November 28, the Consul General at Amsterdam reported that
                    the problem of evacuation of the American colony in the Netherlands had been
                    practically liquidated. (340.1115A/1679, 1748)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
